.TH SYMLINK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
symlink \- create a symbolic link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int symlink(const char* target, const char* path);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a symbolic link at path containing target.  The target need not exist.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR readlink (3crunch),
.BR symlinkat (3crunch),
.BR symlink (2)
